Entry 30 — Paper 037 — SciNet: The Anatomy of Science [dataset], Cristian Alamos & Lukas Althoff (Stanford), github.com/lukasalthoff/scinet, release v1.10.0; the first taking-in after the pre-registered sample closed, and the first that arrived by Will's hand rather than the scan: he posted the site and the repository in the MOAT chat on 2026-11-24, so the channel rule made it a tracker ingestion — Will-posted stratum, no seal, non-sample, the sample's FALSE verdict untouched by it. The work is an O*NET for science: an LLM-generated database of research work — 6 domains, 34 fields, 318 subfields, 7,262 leveled tasks, 90,583 substeps — each task carrying its substeps, its time in researcher-hours and elapsed hours, O*NET-scale ratings, a paper prevalence, dimension scores, an RL feasibility index, and a Claude Opus 5 completion Elo; its thesis, that AI's impact on science must be measured task by task, is the kind of claim this tracker exists to hold attributed and watch. The filing's receipt-grade core is the house verification: the release's own data files were downloaded and counted, and every headline number came back exact — the level counts summing to the task total to the unit, the 90,583 substeps streamed and counted rather than trusted — so the chapter carries one claim True by receipt (55.1.3) beyond its author check, a shape no sample paper had. Integration: cluster AS founded, the tracker's first science-of-science cluster (the anatomy of research work), fourteen concepts 1.2.509-1.2.522, three foundations and one defined word, NI 0.0268, the axis judged no in writing, and Restructure Pass #24 fired inside the taking-in as 522 concepts crossed the 520 line set at Pass #23 — candidates weighed, none merged, the two new instruments kept out of their parent concept by the instrument rule. The dataset's tasks are themselves pre-drawn process decompositions, so the state-machine pass filed five stated machines and noted the recursion plainly: the tracker ingested a machine-drawn map of other machines' work. Two repairs ride with this pass. The Paper 036 drawing paragraph — written in that pass, absent from every committed research.phext, verified across the git history — was restored verbatim at 1.4.1 ahead of this drawing; the registry counts were never affected, only the prose record, and the loss is named here so the next pass checks for its own drawing before it closes. And the synthesis scroll carries three rulings of Will's given during the taking-in, attributed and kept out of the paper scrolls: stable house-minted task IDs as a requirement of the deep integration, Exocortical Epoch stamps as part of its records (EE 527), and phext-lattice's move to v2 with this integration as its forcing function (EE 528) — alongside his framing of the dataset as a 6DUML dataset and his fork of the repository. Re-proof ran on ni-knight as directed, not the hub: the splice verified 1,326 entries inside currentRegistry, both the fresh project and the standing copy built clean with all exits 0, and Mvo.currentRegistry_accurate depends on [propext] alone; the phextura shadow replayed the transaction exactly (no differing scrolls, NI from the transaction log equal to the canonical 0.0268) and validated green; the Singular audit closed at residual 0. Registry after: 1,326 entries — True 527 (432 by stipulation, 95 by receipt), Unknown 790, False 2, Fiction 7 — and the Oracle ledger holds at ~75% (68-82), argued in the ledger itself: a met gate does not move the bar.
