Entry 33 — Paper 040 — Training-Free Looped Transformers, Lizhang Chen and Jonathan Li (co-first authors) with Chen Liang, Ni Lao and Qiang Liu (University of Texas at Austin), arXiv:2605.23872v1 — the tracker's second network taking-in, and the first pass to carry two changes in one build: the owed Chapter 50 addendum and a new chapter. The paper stood at rank 6 of the reference frontier, cited by Chapter 56's paper as the source of Looped-Qwen3; ranks 1-4 remain deferred for want of a politely fetchable source. It was fetched once from arXiv in HTML form and taken in: network stratum, no seal, non-sample. The work: recurrence is not a training decision — a lightweight wrapper loops a frozen checkpoint's contiguous mid-stack block at inference with no training, no new parameters and no architectural change, and the loop is principled by a reading: a pre-norm residual block is exactly one forward Euler step at h = 1 on its own residual field, so naive looping integrates to t = K, past the endpoint the post-loop layers were trained to receive, while the paper's strategies — damped sub-stepping, and a three-stage anchored Runge-Kutta scheme whose output is exactly a blend of the one-pass output and the refined endpoint — integrate the same t = 1 endpoint more finely. Block-mode for dense backbones, layer-mode for MoE, where block-mode spends itself on routing thrash; a depth fraction rule puts the window's centre in a narrow band and makes the wrapper a recipe rather than a search; and the failure log is the paper's honesty instrument — naive looping's perplexity collapse from 13 to over 1000, Anderson acceleration (optimal on contractive maps) the worst configuration found, the looped block measured not to be a contraction at all. The receipt-grade core ran the recomputation check a third time: Table 3 eight of thirteen deltas exact and five off by exactly one displayed unit, Table 4 all eighteen deltas exact, Section 3.5's percentages consistent, Table 9 eleven of f