Entry 42 — Paper 049 — Reasoning Beyond Language: Chen, Zhao, Xia, Lu, Wang, Chen, Zhang, Wang, Li & Shen (The Hong Kong Polytechnic University / Eastern Institute of Technology, Ningbo), 'Reasoning Beyond Language: A Comprehensive Survey on Latent Chain-of-Thought Reasoning': a network taking-in, leg 11 of the reference walk Will directed on 2026-11-24 — the paper stood at rank 14 of the frontier queue, cited in Chapter 56's bibliography, and the queue record was confirmed from queue.jsonl itself before anything was fetched; the record carried the identifier, the title and the full byline, and the held text's byline agrees with it exactly, all ten names in order; one fetch read the arXiv listing, one fetch bought the paper entire (the arXiv HTML of 2505.16782v1, Sections 1-8, limitations, ethics statement and reference list), and two web searches served the author check's web legs; everything else was local — four network operations in all. Versions 2 (1 November 2025) and 3 stand on the listing; the filing reads v1, as the house's passes do — the v1 abstract states the four-perspective taxonomy the body carries, where the current abstract compresses it to the horizontal–vertical axis, and the note at 67.1.4 owns the difference. No correction to the frontier's record was needed. The work is a survey — the first, its authors say, for latent chain-of-thought specifically — and it asks its field to see itself whole: reasoning decoupled from verbalized language, sorted from four perspectives (token-wise strategies; internal mechanisms; analysis and interpretability; applications) and cross-cut by the horizontal axis of the sequence and the vertical axis of depth. Its contents: the discrete markers that scaffold computation, whose structure, on Pfau et al.'s evidence, matters more than their content; the continuous tokens a model feeds itself or receives from an auxiliary module (Coconut, CCoT, CODI, SoftCoT); the mechanisms — computation bought with recurrence, or chains absorbed into representations by training; the analysis wing, which can extract a steering vector from the latent process and read a run's success off its trajectory's geometry without labels, and yet must also record the counter-hypothesis, that the answers were decodable from the early layers all along; and the applications, from text to multimodal generation to recommendation. It closes with its price list: processes no one can supervise, an evaluation gap no metric closes, alignment risks where visibility ends — and five directions it calls future, among them diffusion, which this book already holds as standing ground. Integration founded cluster AW — the field surveyed whole — its first paper, a founding of a new kind for the walk: not a mechanism, not a measurement, but a territory taken as a single object. AT held apart: the survey describes the cluster's whole family in its Section 4.1 and performs no act on any trajectory, and the book files works by what they do. AV held apart: the survey names diffusion a future direction, the opposite of holding that ground. AS held apart: SciNet anatomizes scientific work itself; this survey anatomizes one field's methods and doubts. And the J crossing condition stated at 62.2.2 and weighed at 63.2.2, 64.2.2, 65.2.2 and 66.2.2 was weighed a sixth time and not crossed — the survey consults nothing and issues no verdict; but its analysis wing is a catalogue of the field's verdict-readers, and the catalogue sorts on the condition's own line: Chain of Embedding's self-evaluation, which reads the trajectory's own geometry and judges the run without labels, stands on the trajectory's side; circuit tracing and the logit lens are instruments in an analyst's hand, on the other — and the survey's evaluation gap is the condition's want stated at field scale, the question of whose reading would count left open, with Q231 keeping the seam. Twelve concepts 1.2.659-1.2.670, no held concept revised, no foundation laid (the survey's 