Entry 47 — Paper 054 — ALW: Adaptive Layer-Wise Contrastive Decoding: Zhou, Zhou, Zhang, Li & Zhang of Soochow University — leg fifteen of the network walk, queue rank 18 of the reference frontier, cited by Chapter 56's paper (LoopCD), whose founding contrast this work predates and parallels; and the walk's first pre-processed pass, run as the cost measurement for the house pre-processor (moat-prep). The queue record carried the title, the authors and the year but no identifier; identified by title and authors in two searches, to the Findings of ACL 2025, pages 8506-8524 — the work has no arXiv listing, a first for the walk. Seven network operations in all, single-threaded and at human pace under the netizen rule: two identification searches, the anthology page fetch, one fetch that returned 404 (the preview PDF, a different object from the proceedings PDF), the proceedings PDF fetch itself, and two web searches for the author check. The held material is the proceedings PDF entire, references and appendices included (1,294,842 bytes, sha256 9a53b507…), extracted to text in two forms — a layout form for the tables and a reading-order form for the prose — and read whole. The work: a decoding framework for reasoning whose premise is layer noise, interference accumulating across a network's depth, read as the entropy of each layer's readout through the shared output head — about ten in the shallows, about one at the final layer, in its cases. Against it, self-contrast decoding: the final layer's log-probabilities minus an early layer's, at unit weight, under a plausibility gate inherited from two-model contrastive decoding — with the filing's novelty upstream of the subtraction, in the choice of the layer. The optimal contrastive layer is a property of the prompt, found offline by a quantification strategy that scores gold answers under every candidate contrast in the first half of depth (the noisy half, a bound the paper tests rather than assumes: searching the latter half collapses the gain below plain decoding); the labels accumulate into a prompt–layer database, from which a lightweight classifier — RoBERTa-base in the best configuration, eighteen classes including the embedding layer and a no-contrast label that is the commonest outcome by far — learns to predict the layer from the prompt alone, a tuning-free similarity selector standing as its floor. Measured on five LLaMA models across eight reasoning benchmarks against greedy decoding, DoLa and two-model contrastive decoding, the method's row leads its table at every scale, the gains shrinking as the models grow; it acts only at hesitation points, where the final layer's top candidates stand close, and the paper's own limit stands filed as a concept: the right answer on a wrong path, two arithmetic errors cancelling to a true total, which no sharpening of the distribution can certify away. Integration extended cluster AT — THE TRAJECTORY AS ITS OWN REFERENCE — its eleventh paper, weighed against the live neighbours and held apart from each: AZ, a five-author method paper describing a device, not a family's making, its models another family's used and not described; AY, whose keys the quantification strategy consumes at labelling time without holding or filing any; AV in a line, the paper's denoising a metaphor for subtraction, not a latent being denoised. The border inside AT was weighed, not assumed: the founding papers contrast states of a recurrence, and this one contrasts depths of a single forward pass — held one cluster because the founding concept (1.2.525) has named the intermediate layer of the same dense model as a way of obtaining the weak reference since Paper 038, and the citing paper is AT's founding paper; the axis difference is recorded in the extension, and Q252 keeps open whether the axis is a boundary. And cluster J was weighed — and NOT joined, the walk's first weighing since the crossing. The standing condition (62.2.2, restated 68.2.2): a mechanism co