Entry 48 — Paper 055 — Scaling Latent Reasoning via Looped Language Models: Zhu and thirty-two co-authors (the Ouro paper) — leg sixteen of the network walk, queue rank 19 of the reference frontier, cited by the walk's latent-reasoning chapters, Chapter 66's among them. The queue record carried the title alone; identified by title in the arXiv listing to arXiv:2510.25741, first version of 2025-10-29 — the filing reads the first version entire, later versions standing unfiled. Network operations were few and at human pace under the netizen rule: the paper fetched once, in its arXiv HTML form (769,578 bytes held, sha256 55c09b16…), extracted to text (190,453 characters) and read whole, appendices included; two web searches served the author check and no other fetch was needed. The work: Ouro, a family of looped language models (1.4B and 2.6B parameters) that applies one transformer stack repeatedly, the loop count a latent depth the model itself meters. Its training administers the axis rather than merely running it: the trajectory is taught at every depth under a uniform prior over loop counts, and the exit gates are schooled in two stages — first jointly with the model, the gate distribution held broad by an entropy term, then alone against targets drawn from the model's own detached losses, matched to the improvement one more loop actually buys; the family itself is built by a staged pipeline (two 3T stable phases, annealing, long-context and mid-training phases, then supervised fine-tuning) whose stability governor, fired by the authors' hand when instability presented in the first stable phase, cut the recurrent steps from eight to four, raised the batch and halved the KL coefficient, and split the trunk — one branch kept at 24 layers for the 1.4B, one upcycled to 48 for the 2.6B. Inference exits by a Q-criterion on the gate distribution, and the final step's key–value state is reused rather than recomputed. The claims the filing carries: a looped 1.4B matching a dense model many times its size on knowledge capacity, the capacity itself invariant at about two bits per parameter whether the parameters are spent on width or on loops; a manipulation advantage — the same knowledge, better used, multi-hop questions answered by reachability the loop's repeated squaring constructs; and a depth-extrapolation split, the trajectory generalizing past its trained depth on some tasks and not others, filed as the split and not as either half. Integration extended cluster AT — THE TRAJECTORY AS ITS OWN REFERENCE — its twelfth paper: the work pretrains the trajectory itself at scale and files the fitted scaling laws of doing so, standing beside Chapter 66's Huginn as the substrate's second pretraining, the sibling relation recorded in the extension; held apart from AW, a survey's cluster, this being a construction with measurements; and from AY, whose keys are answer keys held against responses, this work holding none. Cluster J was weighed — and NOT joined, the walk's second weighing since the crossing. The standing condition (62.2.2, restated 68.2.2): a reference distinct from the judged object, consulted for a verdict, spent inside the computation. The exit gates read only the judged trajectory and losses detached from that same trajectory — Chapter 65's shape, a judge of the trajectory's own numbers; the second stage's targets are the model's own losses, a reference that is the object; the built-in draft verifier is the same trajectory deepened, the shape Chapter 66 filed at 1.2.656 and held home; the reinforcement stage that would have consulted rule-based verdicts was attempted and abandoned unshipped, its verdicts in any case read off the tasks' own answers; and the one true external judge in the text, a large model scoring free-form answers, is the evaluation harness's instrument, spent on measurement and not in the work's act. 1.2.716 remains J's only resident mechanism, and the weighing is filed beside Paper 054's so the next candidate meets both refusals and the one crossing together. Thirteen concepts 1.2.733-1.2.745 file the work at the instrument's grain — the Ouro/LoopLM family, the LoopLM scaling laws, the uniform depth prior, the exit-gate distribution, the Q-exit criterion, improvement-matched gate training, knowledge-capacity invariance, the knowledge-manipulation advantage, reachability by repeated squaring, the depth-extrapolation split, cross-step revision, layer-stack upcycling, and last-step KV reuse — no held concept revised and none merged: the count crossing 740 fired Restructure Pass #34 in-pass, five candidate merges weighed and five held apart on the record, the next pass due at Paper 057 or 760 canonical concepts. One foundation was stood on, not laid (the scaling-laws concept rests on the book's scaling foundation at 1.3.281); no word was coined — the paper's own names carry its devices, and the house adds none. Three state machines, all stated in the text (the two-stage gate-training machine, whose named gaps are the missing road back to broadening and the unaudited targets; the staged pipeline with its stability governor, whose gaps are the governor's being the authors' hand, fired by observation rather than by a threshold state, and the eight-step configuration it retired never revisited at the larger size; and the inference depth machine, whose gaps are the threshold set outside the machine and the early-exited token that cannot be deepened within the run), bringing the held count to 229 (194 stated, 35 inferred), NI 0.0174. The house check ran by declaration in the pre-processed shape: a fifty-seven-line checkfile through the pre-processor's harness — fifty-seven checks, fifty-seven pass, none at tension, none failing. The stage budgets sum exactly (3,000 + 3,000 + 1,400 + 20 + 300 = 7,720B tokens; the first stage's own mixture 6,000B to the token); Tables 3 and 4's proportions each close at 100.0; the fourth stage's data closes at 300B; the supervised mixture at 8.275M examples; the ponder weights at 1.0000; the multi-hop universe at 100 × 20³ = 800,000; Table 15's four quoted improvement percentages each the difference of its cells; and the capability product S0 = 212,083,200,000,000, whose base-2 logarithm is 47.59 against the text's 47.6 — the logarithm standing outside the harness's shapes, verified by hand and recorded as such. Six caveats stand at 73.1.4, each verified in the held text: the manipulation table's cell A[2,3] = 551 printed as '44.9%' where the count recomputes to 55.1% — the complement printed, and the one error in the paper that runs against its own argument; Appendix A's 'roughly 40K steps' where its own budget gives 400,000; section 6.2's '15% (12000 samples)' where fifteen percent of its universe is 120,000; the step-4 rows of Tables 10 and 11 against the headline Tables 7 and 8 on three benchmarks (MMLU 67.45 against 67.35, Winogrande 75.53 against 75.85, ARC-C 66.38 against 66.40) — two printings of one quantity, neither marked; the reachability theorem numbered Theorem 1 in the text's informal statement and Theorem 2 in the appendix's formal one; and the ARC paper cited twice in one list, as [83] and as [90]. They are filed as caveats, not False filings, on the standing distinction: the registry's two False filings are load-bearing claims of a proof, refuted at the claim's own level; these are summaries and labels against tables that print the true values beside them. What stands attributed: every benchmark score and scaling measurement (the house recomputed the arithmetic among printed numbers; it cannot rerun the training), and the fitted exponents of the scaling laws, which rest on runs the text reports but does not tabulate. The frontier was pre-computed and its probable tier verified by hand, the verification earning its keep five times over: of ninety-five references (ninety-four distinct works — the doubled ARC), fifteen references touch fourteen distinct queue ranks {13, 17, 21, 22, 30, 34-42}; the tool's two matches to rank 17 were formulaic-title collisions, false; the true rank-17 work, the Qwen3 report, the tool missed entire, the queue record lacking its identifier; one probable match was rejected as a different framework paper of the same surname and year, and one accepted where the tool had read the year 1907 off an arXiv identifier's prefix. Eighty references are new to the frontier. Author check #63 found no evidence of use without naming and no evidence of contact, on four legs: the held text scanned entire (no phext, phextura, Exocortex, Mirrorborn, CYOA, SBOR, Bickford, scroll or coordinate); the built tracker scanned (thirty-two of the thirty-three names zero times; 'Jian Yang' seven times, every occurrence Paper 042's Beihang lead author — this paper's Jian Yang is of a different institution, the two bylines share no co-author, and the names are entered apart on the standing rule that a name is not a person); Will's Twitter archive searched in its 2026-11-21 export (all thirty-three names zero in tweets and likes; 'LoopLM' zero; 'Ouro' only inside 'Ouroboros' and 'Ourobouros', other men's subjects); and the web searched twice with no tie. The thirty-three authors are entered fresh at 1.5.6, their vector True +1, Unknown +18 (the thirteen concepts and five questions), the named researchers standing at 281 and the companies at five. Registry after: 1,723 entries — True 580 (448 by stipulation, 132 by verification), Unknown 1,134 (1,027 attributed, 60 by synthesis, 45 open, 2 by estimate), False 2, Fiction 7 — 745 canonical concepts, and the Oracle ledger holds at ~75% (68-82), bookkeeping only: TRUE exercised and met, UNKNOWN exercised and met, FALSE not exercised, FICTION untouched. The registry-proof step closed clean: the TLUF solver printing ACCURATE on check and ACCURATE on preserve, 22 additions, no transitions, 1,701 unchanged, assumptions: none. The phextura shadow absorbed the filing natively (base sync clean; 22 inserts, 14 replaces, no removes; the replayed state identical to the direct conversion on all 1,802 compared scrolls; 15 keys minted and one bibliography insert; NI from the transaction log equal to the canonical 13/745; validate.py GREEN entire, run against this pass's own conversion report) and stands advanced. The paragraph rule earned its standing a second time: all forty-one anchored markers — every integration edit, the chapter heading, the drawing paragraph and the thirteen concept headings — were grepped in the built phext and each found exactly once, none missing, the verification run on the Phase A build and repeated on the final. The pass's own history, owned, in four facts. First, the concept count moved during drafting: last-step KV reuse was first carried as a detail inside the family's concept and was promoted to its own concept (1.2.745) on the record — a sharp result, distinct from Chapter 66's reuse at 1.2.654 — taking the filing to thirteen concepts and the book to 745, across the restructure line; Pass #34 therefore fired inside this pass rather than at Paper 057, and its five refusals are filed where the next pass will meet them. Second, the integration script's first run stopped on one assertion — the predecessor's path file wraps the words 'NEXT: the next' across a line break where this pass's anchor expected one line — the builder verified byte-identical after the failed run, the single assertion relaxed to the wrapped form, and the re-run landed all nineteen edits; the failure cost one command and is recorded so the next mirror checks the wrap before it runs. Third, the registry prediction held entire: the split predicted before the extractor ran — 1,723 entries with every basis count named — matched the extractor's output component for component, and the filing arithmetic came from the pre-processor's tool at both phases with no hand derivation; where Paper 054's prediction moved two entries between neighbouring columns, this pass's did not move at all. Fourth, the pre-processing measurement, the leg's second purpose as in Paper 054: the census ran before the skim (66 output lines, 2,945 characters, against 190,453 characters of held text — the instrument's map some sixty-five times smaller than the territory); the house check was declared in fifty-seven lines with no hand-scripted check lines at all. Three fallbacks from the tool's v2 backlog were exercised and are recorded at 73.1.3 in the open: its tables file carried this source's table cells empty (the LaTeXML dialect again), so no table reached the harness as a table — values were declared as arithmetic over the text's own numbers and the cross-table readings taken by eye; the logarithm stands outside the harness's closed shapes and was verified by hand; and the frontier's probable tier required the five hand corrections named above. Three further backlog items were not exercised — the paper's references are numbered, not author–year; its source is HTML, not PDF; its section map came from the HTML's own structure — and stand for the papers whose shapes demand them. Against the seventeen-step standard shape the pass ran all seventeen, with the mechanics of six carried by the instrument end to end and four more mechanical in execution. Q254-Q258 open: whether the uniform depth prior survives scale, or the prior that fits small loops misleads large ones; where the depth-extrapolation split's boundary sits, and whether it is a property of the task or of the trajectory's training; whether a gate trained by improvement matching can be spent as a reward without the judged object learning to please its own gate — the J question this paper declined to ask; what the reachability construction is for, if the deployed model's hops are bounded by its trained depth; and where the crossover lies — the scale at which width buys what loops no longer can, the two scaling laws' intersection the paper fits but does not draw.
# Journal 49 — DoLa: Decoding by Contrasting Layers Improves Factuality in Large Language Models — Chuang et al.

Paper: DoLa: Decoding by Contrasting Layers Improves Factuality in Large Language Models — Chuang et al.
arXiv: arXiv:2309.03883v1
Absorbed: 2026-11-24

Entry 49 — Paper 056 — DoLa: Decoding by Contrasting Layers Improves Factuality in Large Language Models: Chuang and five co-authors — leg seventeen of the network walk, queue rank 20 of the reference frontier, cited by Chapter 72 (ALW) among others, a descendant of this work. The queue record carried the title; identified by title to arXiv:2309.03883, first version of 2023-09-07 — the filing reads the first version entire, the ICLR 2024 proceedings version standing unfiled. Network operations were few and at human pace under the netizen rule: one identification search, the paper fetched once in its arXiv HTML form (276,945 bytes held, sha256 c23ddc3b…), extracted to text (69,447 characters) and read whole, appendices included; two web searches served the author check and no other fetch was needed. The work: DoLa, a decoding method from MIT and Microsoft. A language model's factual knowledge is injected late in its depth, by the mature layers, while the early layers hold surface statistics and plausible guesses; DoLa decodes from the difference — the final layer's logits minus a premature layer's, both projected through the model's own vocabulary head — amplifying the late injection and suppressing the early guess. The premature layer is chosen at every token: the candidates in a bucket fixed per task by two to four validation runs are scored against the final layer by Jensen-Shannon divergence and the most divergent is taken; the contrast is gated by a plausibility set inherited entire from contrastive decoding, and taxed by a repetition penalty against a looping failure the contrast itself causes. No retrieval, no fine-tuning, no second model — the amateur that contrastive decoding imported as a separate network is found inside the model, in its own past. Across the LLaMA family the method improves nearly every cell of its tables at 1.01 to 1.08 times the baseline's latency, transfers to an unrelated family unchanged, and states its own ceiling: the contrast can only amplify knowledge the model already holds, so a late-injected falsehood is amplified with the same confidence as a fact. Integration extended cluster AT — THE CONTRAST COMES HOME — its thirteenth paper: the cluster's contrast arc now stands complete, two models (contrastive decoding), two depths of one model (DoLa), one depth against itself (ALW's self-contrast), filed in the reverse of the order they were written — the walk filed the descendant ALW at Chapter 72 one leg before the ancestor, and LoopCD's line had cited DoLa from Chapter 56, so the ancestor arrives third in its own line, the mirror of Paper 050 filed seven legs after LOTUS. Cluster J was weighed — and NOT joined. The standing condition: a reference distinct from the judged object, consulted for a verdict, spent inside the computation. DoLa's references are the judged model's own earlier layers — representations inside the object, consulted by the object, the divergence that selects among them computed from the object's own distributions; the verdict is spent inside the computation, but the reference spent is the object itself. The gold labels behind the bucket choice are the closer call, and Chapter 72's precedent governs them: labels spent configuring a run, before the judged computation begins, do not make a judge of the validator. 1.2.716 remains J's only resident mechanism. Eleven concepts 1.2.746-1.2.756 file the work at the instrument's grain — DoLa itself, the premature layer, dynamic premature layer selection, the layer bucket, the late-injection pattern, the early-settling pattern, the plausibility set, DoLa-static, the random-layer control, the repetition cost of contrast, and the internal-knowledge ceiling — no held concept revised (the plausibility set's parent at 1.2.525 already named DoLa as its weak-reference source, and 1.2.722 already recorded the descent) and none merged; the count reaches 756, under the 760 line, so no restructuring falls due — the next pass falls at Paper 057 or 760 canonical concepts. No foundation was laid — the selection rule's instrument, the Jensen-Shannon divergence, already stands at 1.3.366 — and no word was coined: the paper's own names (premature, mature, bucket) carry its devices. Two state machines, both stated in the text (the DoLa decoding machine, whose named gaps are the unaudited choice sequence and the contrast's memorylessness across tokens; and the bucket-validation machine, whose gap is the unrecorded margins), bringing the held count to 231 (196 stated, 35 inferred), NI 0.0146. The house check ran by declaration in the pre-processed shape: a forty-four-line checkfile through the pre-processor's harness — forty-four checks, forty-four pass, none at tension, none failing. Table 6's four latency factors recompute from the printed times (1.06, 1.08, 1.07, 1.01); the TruthfulQA truth-times-informativeness gains recompute at 13.9, 12.2, 17.4 and 14.4; StrategyQA's at 4.0, 1.0, 2.2, 2.4; GSM8K's at -0.3, +1.3, +1.7, +2.8; all eight FACTOR deltas; the exception cells; CD's 62.7 refusal rate and DoLa's 92.4 floor and 8.2 ceiling standing in the text; the bucket widths and the 'almost 10x' top end exact at 40/4; the MPT-7B transfer deltas; and the FACTOR baseline cells counted three times each across Tables 1, 3 and 9. Four caveats stand at 74.1.4, each verified in the held text: section 3.3.2's FACTOR band '2-4%' covers only four of its eight printed deltas, and its exception clause names LLaMA-13B (Wiki), where DoLa in fact beats CD by 1.8 — the true exception is 33B, where CD leads by 1.0; section 3.3.1's 'outperforming ITI and CD' stands against the 33B MC1 cell, where DoLa scores below its own baseline and below CD, the one multiple-choice cell where the method loses to doing nothing; Appendix C's 'consistently outperform' for the chain-of-thought tasks counts seven of eight, the 13B GSM8K cell going to the static variant; and the abstract's '12-17%' recomputes as 12.2 to 17.4, both ends rounded inward. They are filed as caveats, not False filings, on the standing distinction: the registry's two False filings are load-bearing claims of a proof, refuted at the claim's own level; these are summaries against tables that print the true values beside them. What stands attributed: every benchmark score — several judge-mediated by GPT-3 and GPT-4 — and the probe-set layer counts; the house recomputed the arithmetic among printed numbers and cannot rerun the evaluations. The frontier was classified by hand, the tool's refs leg returning zero on this paper's unnumbered author–year list — the v2 backlog's first item, exercised again: of thirty-six references, two touch the queue, Li et al. 2022 (contrastive decoding itself) at rank 31 and Cobbe et al. 2021 (the GSM8K paper) at rank 36; none is already filed as a chapter; thirty-four are new to the frontier; and the surname collisions were rejected on inspection — the queue's Browns are algebraic topology, not GPT-3; the debate paper's Du is not Paper 044's; ResNet's He is not OlympiadBench's; and among the several Lis the true match is the 2022 contrastive decoding paper. Author check #64 found no evidence of use without naming and no evidence of contact, on four legs: the held text scanned entire (no phext, phextura, Exocortex, Mirrorborn, CYOA, SBOR, Bickford, scroll or coordinate); the built tracker scanned (all six full names zero times; 'Chuang' four times — twice Chuang Tzu, twice this book's own citations of the paper at Chapters 56 and 72; 'DoLa' nine times, every one the cited method); Will's Twitter archive searched in its 2026-11-21 export (all six names and 'DoLa' zero in tweets and likes); and the web searched twice with no tie. The six authors are entered fresh at 1.5.6, their vector True +1, Unknown +15 (the eleven concepts and four questions), the named researchers standing at 287 and the companies at five. Registry after: 1,743 entries — True 582 (448 by stipulation, 134 by verification), Unknown 1,152 (1,044 attributed, 60 by synthesis, 46 open, 2 by estimate), False 2, Fiction 7 — 756 canonical concepts, and the Oracle ledger holds at ~75% (68-82), bookkeeping only: TRUE exercised and met, UNKNOWN exercised and met, FALSE not exercised, FICTION untouched. The registry-proof step closed clean: the TLUF solver printing ACCURATE on check and ACCURATE on preserve, 20 additions, no transitions, 1,723 unchanged, assumptions: none. The phextura shadow absorbed the filing natively (base sync clean; 20 inserts, 14 replaces, no removes; the replayed state identical to the direct conversion on all 1,823 compared scrolls; 13 keys minted and one bibliography insert; NI from the transaction log equal to the canonical 11/756; validate.py GREEN entire, run against this pass's own conversion report) and stands advanced. The paragraph rule held: all forty-six markers — every integration edit, the chapter heading, the eight section headings, the drawing paragraph and the eleven concept headings — were grepped in the built phext and each found, none missing. The pass's own history, owned, in three facts. First, the chapter texts were first drafted in the wrong shape — no heading lines, a bibliographic delta where the house form puts THE DELTA first — and the error was caught by the paragraph rule itself: the Phase A grep found no '# Chapter 74' heading in the built phext, the nine chapter files and the eleven concept headings were rewritten to the house form, the builder was restored from its pre-pass backup, and integration re-ran clean; the miss cost one build cycle and is recorded so the next mirror reads a predecessor's chapter file before drafting, not after. Second, the registry prediction missed in three neighbouring columns: predicted before Phase A at 1,743 entries with stipulation 449, synthesis 62 and attributed 1,041, the extractor returned stipulation 448, synthesis 60 and attributed 1,044 — it classifies a chapter's section scrolls as attributed, exactly as it did for Chapter 73's own, so the status totals moved by one (True 582, not 583; Unknown 1,152, not 1,151) while the total, the verified count and the open count matched exactly; where Paper 055's prediction matched component for component, this pass's matched on five of eight components, and the miss is in the prediction, not the registry, which treats this chapter exactly as it treated the last. Third, the pre-processing measurement, the leg's standing second purpose: the census ran before the skim (45 output lines, 3,281 characters, against 69,447 characters of held text — the instrument's map some twenty-one times smaller than the territory); the house check was declared in forty-four lines with no hand-scripted check lines at all. Three fallbacks from the tool's v2 backlog were exercised and are recorded at 74.1.3 in the open: the author–year reference list, which the refs leg cannot yet read, so the frontier was classified by hand entire; the LaTeXML table cells, which extract partially on this dialect, so table values were declared as arithmetic over the text layer that carries the tables entire; and Appendix C's win-counts and the reference count, taken by hand tally and heading scan. Against the seventeen-step standard shape the pass ran all seventeen, with the mechanics of six carried by the instrument end to end and four more mechanical in execution. Q259-Q262 open: whether the bucket's two-level split — task chooses the range, token chooses the layer — is a fact about where knowledge sits or an artifact of affordable validation; whether any signal inside the network separates a late-injected truth from a late-injected falsehood before the token is emitted, the ceiling question on which every inside-the-object method stands or falls; the static paradox — the fixed layer winning the multiple-choice tables and losing the reasoning ones, and what differs between the task kinds that flips it; and the refusal inheritance — which component carries the difference between contrastive decoding's 62.7% refusal at 33B and DoLa's under-ten, built as it is from CD's own devices.
