Entry 52 — Paper 059 — Autoguidance: Karras, Aittala, Kynkäänniemi, Lehtinen, Aila & Laine — leg twenty of the network walk, queue rank 23 of the reference frontier, the paper Chapter 56's paper (LoopCD) cites in the lineage its concept states. The queue record carried the title and the six authors but no identifier; identified by title in one search — 'Guiding a Diffusion Model with a Bad Version of Itself', arXiv:2406.02507 — and held entire in its v3 form (19 Dec 2024; v1 of 4 Jun 2024; NeurIPS 2024): the arXiv HTML (493,660 bytes) and its text layer held beside it, one fetch at human pace under the netizen rule. The work: the NVIDIA and Aalto group's autoguidance — guide a diffusion model not with an unconditional model, as classifier-free guidance does, but with a bad version of itself: a denoiser trained on the same task, the same conditioning and the same data, degraded by reduced capacity and shorter training, so that the difference between the two models' results, amplified and spent at every step of the sampling trajectory, pushes samples away from the errors the two models share. The skim foresaw the shape before the full reading: cluster AV — the denoising-trajectory country founded at Chapter 63 — was the natural home, the paper's iterated object being a denoising path travelled once per sample; and the J question was visible from the abstract onward, the method consulting a distinct reference inside the computation. The reading confirmed the first and sharpened the second into the filing's centre. Integration extended cluster AV to two papers — its second resident, and its first from outside latent reasoning: where LaDiR's trajectory forms its sample unsteered, this one is corrected at every step by a second model's reading of it, and what the extension adds to the country is steering itself. Cluster J was weighed — the walk's sixth weighing since the crossing at Chapter 71 — on the distinction the leg's brief named, steering signal against verdict, and NOT joined: J's standing condition wants a verdict whose evidence lies beyond the judged object, and the twin renders none — the shared-error difference is a vector field, not a score; it cannot be thresholded, it ranks nothing, it accepts and rejects nothing, and where the two models agree it vanishes, which a verdict never does when its judge agrees with the judged. The holding is written to be falsifiable — a family member whose guiding signal is read out as a score and consumed as one crosses on the spot — and Q271 leaves the edge open. Eight concepts 1.2.776-1.2.783 file the work at its own grain — autoguidance, the bad version of itself, the shared-error difference, compatible degradations, the quality gap inside CFG, disentangled guidance, guidance at every noise level, and the post-hoc EMA pair — no held concept revised and none merged. The filing crossed the concept line, and Restructuring Pass #36 fell due and was run in-pass: five merges weighed and held apart (autoguidance into contrastive decoding — kin named, concepts separate, the family's standing practice; the quality gap into autoguidance — a diagnosis is not the construction it motivates; the twin into the difference — artifact against signal, as the latent thought space stands apart from the trajectory; guidance at every noise level into the trajectory — a property of guidance is not the path; compatible degradations into the twin — a property of a pairing, not of one of its relata), no splits, nothing retired, the next trigger standing at Paper 060 or 800 canonical concepts. No foundation was laid and no word was coined. Two state machines, both stated in the work — the guided sampling machine, its gaps that no state examines the pair's compatibility, none records the guide's provenance, and none reads the sample being formed; and the guide-manufacture machine, its gaps that the search, not the guide, is the machine's real cost, and that no state selects the guide by a rule — bringing the held