Entry 58 — Paper 065 — A Framework for Few-Shot Language Model Evaluation: Gao, Tow, Abbasi, Biderman, Black, DiPofi, Foster, Golding, Hsu, Le Noac'h, Li, McDonell, Muennighoff, Ociepa, Phang, Reynolds, Schoelkopf, Skowron, Sutawika, Tang, Thite, Wang, Wang & Zou — leg twenty-six of the network walk, queue rank 29 of the reference frontier, cited by Chapter 56, whose bibliography is the looped-transformer neighborhood entire — and this filing is the walk's strangest return, because the cited work is not a paper in that neighborhood at all but the instrument the whole neighborhood is measured with: the Language Model Evaluation Harness, the program through which a large share of the book's filed scores were produced, standing in the bibliography of the cluster's founding survey like a tool left in a photograph of the work it enabled. The queue record carried no identifier at all — a bare title and a year — so the identification is part of the filing's record: the title is the harness's own, Chapter 56's reference [14] cites it with a truncated venue, and the version of record is the work's archival deposit, Zenodo record 10256836, version 0.4.0, deposited 2023-12-04 under DOI 10.5281/zenodo.10256836 — settled not by the search that first misled (the deposit hides under its software title; a remembered DOI named a sibling work) but by the versions list under the work's concept DOI, identity verified by content, per the walk's standing lesson. Held entire: the deposit's archive, 1,805,987 bytes, verified against the record's own stated md5 before a single count was taken — the artifact checksummed by its own record, the strongest identity the walk has held — and read as what it is, a program of 2,442 files whose paper is its README, 17,711 bytes, held verbatim. The work: twenty-four authors of the EleutherAI collective and its orbit, building the examination hall the field now files through — a library of tasks written as configuration files rather than code, a model reduced to three requests any backend can answer, few-shot examples drawn from a seeded sampler so a score can be re-drawn exactly, multiple choice graded by length-normalized likelihood, training corpora passed through a decontamination filter before scores are trusted, and every number published with a bootstrap error bar as part of the score. The skim foresaw the cluster question open — the brief named AY and AT and left the call to the paper's own mechanism — and the reading settled it on the precedent the book already held: Paper 057 filed the examination's apparatus as concepts of the examination's country, and the harness is that apparatus with the grader detached from every table and made general, so cluster AY is extended, its fourth paper, the country gaining its instrument; the alternative, a country of infrastructure founded on one work, was weighed and declined under the territory rule of 77.2.2, and stands reweighable the day a second such work arrives. Cluster J was weighed — the walk's twelfth weighing since the crossing at Chapter 71 — and NOT joined, on the shape the book knows best: the harness consults the answer key at grading, after the judged computation has ended, and no verdict of its is spent inside any computation it judges; it is the shape of Paper 057's filing at program scale, and 1.2.716 remains J's only resident mechanism. Seven concepts file the work at its own grain — 1.2.821 the evaluation harness, 1.2.822 the task as configuration, 1.2.823 the three requests, 1.2.824 the length-normalized choice, 1.2.825 the seeded few-shot draw, 1.2.826 the decontamination pass, 1.2.827 the bootstrap error bar — no foundation was laid (the hall's parts are instruments, and the book's foundations are statements; the nearest candidate, that a benchmark is a configuration, is already the concept's own claim), no held concept was revised, and no word was coined. Three state machines, all stated — the evaluation machine, its gaps that no state compares