Entry 59 — Paper 066 — Is Your Code Generated by ChatGPT Really Correct? Rigorous Evaluation of Large Language Models for Code Generation: Liu, Xia, Wang & Zhang — leg twenty-seven of the network walk, queue rank 30 of the reference frontier, cited by Chapter 56, whose bibliography is the looped-transformer neighborhood entire — and where the previous leg returned the instrument the neighborhood is measured with, this one returns the audit of the neighborhood's most-quoted examination: EvalPlus, the work that took HumanEval — the code table the field reads its rankings off — and asked whether its verdicts survive being computed properly. The queue record carried no identifier at all, a bare title, so the identification is part of the filing's record: the title is the EvalPlus paper's own, Chapter 56's bibliography names EvalPlus at this rank, and the version of record is the third, arXiv:2305.01210v3 of 2023-10-30, the work's NeurIPS 2023 form, settled from the arXiv record's own version list — v1 of 2023-05-02, v2 of 2023-06-12, v3 the version the proceedings carry. Held entire: the arXiv HTML of the third version, 315,936 bytes, fetched once and read entire, its extracted text 59,508 characters; and the work's artifact entire — the HumanEvalPlus dataset itself, drawn from the release address the work's own code names, in the two states that bracket the version of record, packed 2023-09-30 and 2023-11-13, held by their hashes, with the work's code held at two tags so the dataset's version pins could be read in the code itself: the September code pins the earlier state, the November code the later, and the paper of October sits between them. The work: four authors of the Illinois and Lehigh line, heirs of a decade of fuzzing, turning the fuzzer's discipline on the field's favorite examination — a model that has read the ground-truth solutions writes the seed inputs, type-aware mutation grows them for an hour a problem until each problem holds on the order of a thousand, input contracts fence the domain the ground truths themselves declare, and a differential oracle grades each candidate by running it against the reference implementation rather than against any stored answer; and then the audit turns on the key itself, a second implementation written to cross-check the first, finding eighteen of the 164 ground truths defective — five whose solutions solve the wrong problem, ten whose canonical forms fail their own contracts or the agreed semantics, three not well-formed as programs — so that the base table's key was wrong in eleven percent of its problems before a single candidate was graded. At the deepened depth the field's orderings move: pass rates fall by up to a printed 28.9 percent, two open models pass ChatGPT on the hardened table while trailing it on the base, and small models overtake larger ones — the ranking the field quoted was, in part, a property of the examination's shallowness, 9.6 tests where the hardened table holds 764.1. The skim foresaw the cluster question open between AY and a code-country kinship, and the reading settled it on the country's own definition and the precedent of the leg before: the deliverable is a table — fixed problems, computed verdicts, published as data — so cluster AY is extended, its fifth paper, the examination's audit of itself filed in the country of the examinations; the infrastructure founding deferred at Chapter 83 was reweighed in earnest on this second apparatus work and declined again, the two works' centers of mass differing — the harness apparatus with a library attached, this work a table with an apparatus attached — and the condition that reopens the founding stands restated at 84.2.2 for a third work whose center of mass is apparatus itself. No code country stands in the book to join: the code examinations themselves, HumanEval and MBPP, are queue nodes at ranks 34 and 35, this work's own base tables, and a country is not founded from the citing side. Cluster J was weighed — the walk's thirteenth weighing since the crossing at Chapter 71 — and NOT joined, and the weighing is the filing's sharpest instrument: the oracle's reference is as distinct from the judged object as a reference can be, its evidence beyond the judged object entire, its spending verdict-spending in form — and still it does not cross, because the verdict is spent at grading, upon artifacts of a computation already ended, and nothing it returns is spent inside the judged model's own run; the filing therefore narrows Q288 on the record — neither the spending's form nor the evidence's source carries the boundary alone; the locus does — and 1.2.716 remains J's only resident mechanism. Eight concepts file the work at its own grain — 1.2.828 the differential oracle, 1.2.829 the model-written seed, 1.2.830 type-aware mutation, 1.2.831 the input contract, 1.2.832 the killing requirement, 1.2.833 the distilled suite, 1.2.834 the fallible ground truth, 1.2.835 the insufficiency reversal — and one foundation was laid, 1.3.379 set cover, the book's first, standing behind the reduction's greedy rule; no held concept was revised, and no word was coined. Three state machines, all stated — the input generation machine, its gaps that no state measures coverage of the input space and the filter's discards are nowhere counted; the differential evaluation machine, its gaps that the machine believes the ground truth entire and its time bound folds speed into correctness with no state separating them; and the reduction machine, its gap that no state re-derives the suite for a new model family — bringing the held count to 256 (219 stated, 37 inferred), NI 8/835 = 0.0096. The house check ran against the artifact itself, the house's pattern for held data: thirty-five declarations through the pre-processor's harness, thirty-five PASS, no tension, no failure — the census computed from the artifact entire in both held states: 164 tasks with their nine keys; base inputs summing 1,570, averaging 9.5732, median 7, running 1 to 105; plus inputs summing 123,741 in the earlier state and 123,739 in the later, median 974, running 2 to 1,000 in both; totals 125,311 and 125,309, averages 764.0915 and 764.0793 — Table 2's printed row recomputed to the decimal from the artifact itself, in both states, the two states differing in exactly two inputs across the whole dataset, one problem's plus count moving 451 to 449 and one canonical solution rewritten; the contract markers counted present in all 164 rows in both states, against the paper's printed 83; the defect arithmetic 5 + 10 + 3 = 18 of 164; the population 18 + 8 = 26 configurations; the printed ratios recomputed at 47.5 and 79.6; and Table 3's percentage column recomputed pair by pair — exact for the three open flagships, 18.54, 17.57 and 14.08 percent — while the two commercial rows fail, ChatGPT's printed 12.6 recomputing to 13.39 and GPT-4's printed 13.1 to 13.80 from the table's own printed cells, and the column's up-to maxima recompute under no reading of the printed cells, carried as attributed to unrounded sample-level data this desk does not hold. Three pieces stand as named hand work: the artifact census itself, a held script over the dataset files in both states, the declarations reading its counts; the Table 3 analysis, a held script over tables extracted by hand — the pre-processor's own table extraction returning empty cells on this paper's HTML dialect, the fallback extractor of Paper 064's pass supplying the tables entire, the failure recorded for the instrument's backlog; and a probe of the check harness itself, which found its jsonl counter reading string-encoded integers where the artifact writes JSON numbers — probe-verified on the node, recorded in the chapter, the declarations routed to fields the counter reads truly. No model was run from this desk; every score the work exists to produce stands attributed. The caveats at 84.1.4 are the artifact judging its paper: the two commercial percentages that fail their own table's cells; the up-to maxima no reading recomputes; a stray 774.8 standing in the prose where the table and the artifact both say 764.1; the contracts the paper counts at 83 standing in the artifact at 164, unreconciled anywhere in the work; the mini suite's own drift, its recomputed average 16.34 and maximum 109 against the printed 16.1 and 110; a living artifact under a fixed name, its two held states differing in exactly the two inputs the paper's own appendix confesses to fixing; the abstract swelling across the work's three versions as the claims grew; and the commercial rows standing as the table's least-sampled, their verdicts resting on the fewest generations of any rows in it. Author check #74 found no evidence of use without naming, on four legs: the held paper text scanned entire (no phext, phextura, Exocortex, Mirrorborn, CYOA, SBOR or Bickford, and the check's two ordinary-word terms occurring zero times each — the work contains none of Will's terms in any sense); the built tracker scanned for all four names, zero each, the surnames crowds entire — Liu 116 times, Wang 95, Zhang 120, Xia 44, every one another person or a byline, the group's own fuzzing line standing in this paper's reference list and nowhere in the book; Will's Twitter archive searched entire as data, 77,512 texts (all four names, the work's title and 'EvalPlus' itself zero in tweets and likes); and the web searched twice with no tie. All four authors are new to the book; the named researchers stand at 359 and the companies at six, 320 named across the sixty-six papers; each of the four stands at True +1, False +0, Unknown +12 (the eight concepts and Q299-Q302), Fiction +0. Registry after: 1,916 entries — True 606 (452 by stipulation, 154 by verification), Unknown 1,301 (1,183 attributed, 60 by synthesis, 56 open, 2 by estimate), False 2, Fiction 7 — 835 canonical concepts, and the Oracle ledger holds at ~75% (68-82), bookkeeping only. No restructuring fell due; the next trigger stands where Pass #38 set it, Paper 070 or 840 canonical concepts. The registry-proof step closed clean: the TLUF solver printing ACCURATE on check and ACCURATE on preserve — 18 additions, no transitions, 1,898 unchanged, assumptions: none — and the solver's counts, the extractor's and moat-prep arith's agree exactly at every stage, three instruments on one registry. The phextura shadow absorbed the pass natively (base sync clean; 18 inserts, 14 replaces, no removes; the replayed state identical to the direct conversion on all 2,006 compared scrolls, the compared difference empty; 11 keys minted and one bibliography insert; NI from the transaction log equal to the canonical 8/835 exactly; validate.py GREEN against this pass's conversion report, named explicitly on the command line, the shadow advanced before the run) and stands advanced. The paragraph rule held: all forty-six markers — every integration edit, the chapter heading, the section headings, the drawing paragraph, the eight concept headings, the foundation heading, the four question headings, J's holding line and the novelty line — were grepped in the built phext and each found, none missing, on the Phase A build and again on the final. The pass's own history, owned, in three facts. First, the pre-registered registry prediction landed EXACT on every component — 1,916 entries; True 606 (452 by stipulation, 154 by verification); Unknown 1,301 (attributed 1,183, synthesis 60, open 56, estimate 2); False 2; Fiction 7 — the sixth consecutive fully exact split, the streak now running from Paper 057; and beside it the pass's instruments agreed everywhere they were made to meet: two dataset states reproducing one table to the decimal, three registry instruments on one count, the transaction log's novelty index equal to the canonical to the last digit. Second, the pass's one red moment was mine and is recorded plainly: the extractor edit's first run broke the extractor — my evidence anchor matched the tail of an override's long evidence string instead of the evidence dictionary's entry, the same closing words standing in two homes, and the insert landed inside the wrong structure; the extractor was restored from the pre-pass copy taken before the edit, the anchor re-cut on a tail that occurs exactly once, and the re-run landed clean — the identity lesson of the walk's twenty-fourth leg in a new dress: an anchor, like an input, is verified by its whole context or not at all. Third, the paper's artifact proved more honest than its prose in a way the walk has not met before: the numbers the artifact could speak for — the test counts, the contract markers, the defect arithmetic — recomputed exactly, in two states at once; the numbers only the prose speaks for — the commercial percentages, the up-to maxima, the stray average — are precisely the ones that fail or cannot be recomputed; a work that publishes its artifact entire has, perhaps without intending it, told its readers which of its claims to trust, and the filing's caveats simply read that telling back. Q299-Q302 open: whether a reference implementation can be audited without another reference of the same kind, the regress this work stops after one round; whether a model grades itself on a curve when it has stocked the examination's seeds, the seed-writer sitting among the judged with its blind spots inherited as the examination's frontier; whether a distilled suite's equivalence is a property of the suite or of the pair of suite and population, a later model wrong in new places passing precisely where the full suite would have caught it; and whether the insufficiency reversal replicates on the second table, MBPP, the queue's rank 35 — one table, however deep, being one witness, and the walk's own road now running at the base tables themselves, ranks 34 and 35 both standing in the queue this filing's frontier names.
# Journal 60 — Contrastive Decoding: Open-ended Text Generation as Optimization — Li, Holtzman, Fried, Liang, Eisner, Hashimoto, Zettlemoyer & Lewis

Paper: Contrastive Decoding: Open-ended Text Generation as Optimization — Li, Holtzman, Fried, Liang, Eisner, Hashimoto, Zettlemoyer & Lewis
arXiv: arXiv:2210.15097v2 (submitted 2022-10-27, last revised 2023-07-10)
Absorbed: 2026-11-25

Entry 60 — Paper 067 — Contrastive Decoding: Open-ended Text Generation as Optimization: Li, Holtzman, Fried, Liang, Eisner, Hashimoto, Zettlemoyer & Lewis — leg twenty-eight of the network walk, queue rank 31 of the reference frontier, cited by Chapter 56 — the last of the contrast line's members to be filed, and its founder. Every other leg of this walk has taken in a paper the book reached forward toward; this one reached backward, to the ancestor the whole line descends from, and the filing's interest was never whether the ancestor would join the family — it was what the ancestor would say about the family's account of it. The queue record carried a bare title and no identifier, and the identification earned its keep in the first hour: my first candidate arXiv number, assembled from memory of the paper's season, belonged to a coding-theory paper on CR fields — a wrong door opened confidently. The title search found the true record: arXiv:2210.15097, second version of July 2023, the ACL form. I record the wrong guess here because the pass's first lesson is in it: the queue's silence about identifiers is not a gap to be filled from memory, and the desk's standing rule — verify identity by content, never by name — caught in minutes what confidence would have filed entire.

The skim foresaw the shape correctly and the substance wrong, which is the more instructive failure. Foreseen: cluster AT extended through the contrast line, the founding shape's first filing, J weighed and not joined, eight or so concepts around the amateur and the constraint. All of that landed. What the skim did not foresee — what three years of the book's own record actively concealed — was that the founding concept itself, 1.2.525, imported at Paper 038 from a descendant's lineage statement and carried since as the family's root, states a rule the founding paper never wrote. The weighted form, z' = z_s + w(z_s − z_w), with its tunable strength, is the descendants' generalization: LoopCD carries a w, CAD a ratio of alphas, CFG a gamma, and the reasoning namesake's abstract describes the ancestor's own method as 'a weighted difference in likelihood'. The ancestor's rule is the unweighted difference of log-probabilities, weight exactly one, searched by beam — and its protection is not a leash on the step but a gate at the door: the plausibility constraint, V_head, the set of tokens the expert itself rates within a factor of the best, outside which the contrast may not look. Remove the gate and the method does not weaken, it collapses — MAUVE 0.01, perplexity two hundred thousand, diversity a perfect and meaningless 1.0 — because the ungated difference's favourite text is a token at probability 3e-9 whose contrast is 10.6. The descendants each dropped the gate and took up a strength instead, silently, and none of their chapters remarks the exchange. The revision of 1.2.525 is this leg's first finding and its real product: dated, sourced, the true parts of the held scroll preserved, the weighted form reassigned to its actual authors. A tracker that cannot correct its root concept against the root text is a scrapbook; this one can, and did, and the TLUF preserve accepted the filing with the revision inside its unchanged count, the standing never having moved.

The ancestor kept giving back more than its descendants kept. Its last appendix trains the amateur — beamprefix, a small model prefix-tuned on the expert's own beam-search degeneration — which is the one-model turn the book credited to DoLa and CAD and CFG, present in embryo in 2022: the weak pole manufactured from the strong one's behaviour rather than borrowed. Its other appendix proves the objective's argmax is pointwise mutual information with the expert's authorship — distinguishability, not quality — the identity the book filed at Chapter 79 as CAD's frame, reassigned here to its true root, with maximum probability, n-gram blocking and MMI falling out as special cases. And its limitations section states, as a warning, what Chapter 81 would restate as a law: where both models are good, the contrast has nothing to subtract. The line's whole philosophy was in the founding text; the descendants kept the arithmetic and dropped the two readings — the less-informed listener, distinguishability — that said what the arithmetic means. Q303 through Q306 stand where the dropped pieces fell: the gate against the leash, the trained amateur against the borrowed one, distinguishability against quality, and the rhyme — the failure-mode mirror every contrast spends and none measures.

The instruments behaved the way this walk has taught me to expect: honestly, at their stated edges. The pre-processor's references leg returned zero on the unnumbered author–year bibliography — backlog item one, met before — and the named fallback classified all twenty-nine references; its frontier raised two probable matches, and hand-verification rejected both as surname collisions, one of them a representation-theory paper sharing nothing with its candidate but a common name. The tables arm worked — twenty-five tables — with the merged-cell dialect shifting cells in four, read against the text. The check harness refused my first four ratio declarations twice, once for parentheses and once for unspaced operators, each time with a form error that named the fault; the grammar tokenizes on whitespace and admits no grouping, and the honest workaround — declaring the sum of the per-row ratios against six times the printed mean — is also the more faithful declaration, since the paper's headline is a mean of ratios and the sum is what its table supports. That is instrument finding seven for the efficiency backlog: the arith grammar wants a parentheses arm, or its documentation wants the whitespace rule stated where a filer will meet it. The house check itself: seventeen declarations, seventeen pass; ten hand checks, ten pass — the four headline ratios recompute at their printed precision, the diversity identity holds over fifty-seven rows, the cross-table agreements are exact — and the ablation appendix prints its Context Ablation row twice, the second copy wearing the V_head Ablation's name and contradicting the main table's collapse. The ancestor's own evidence for its gate's necessity is a photocopy of its neighbour; the necessity survives on the main table alone, which is unambiguous. I have filed three photocopied columns in four legs now — Sanchez's duplicated code column, this duplicated row — and the pattern deserves its sentence: in this literature, an ablation table is a claim about runs, and some of its rows are claims about other rows.

The filing crosses the line the book set for itself: 843 canonical concepts against Pass #38's trigger of 840, so the restructure falls due — and per the brief it does not run here. The paper is filed, the trigger stands reported, and the restructure waits for its own pass with its own brief, the discipline this walk has kept since Pass #38 was itself run in-pass at Paper 065 and set this trigger. The pre-registered split landed exact for the seventh consecutive pass — seventeen additions in the classifier's own terms, predicted before Phase A and met to the entry — and the phextura transaction log's novelty figure, computed from its own inserts and its one concept replace, equals the canonical (8 + 0.5)/843 to the last digit: two instruments that have never met agreeing on what this filing was. The oracle ledger is untouched by all of it, as it should be: the walk's seventy-fifth author check found no evidence, the axis was never in this paper, and the book is larger by one ancestor and one correction — the correction worth more than the ancestor, since the ancestor was always coming and the error was ours.
# Journal 61 — Classifier-Free Diffusion Guidance — Ho & Salimans

Paper: Classifier-Free Diffusion Guidance — Ho & Salimans
arXiv: arXiv:2207.12598v1 (submitted 2022-07-26)
Absorbed: 2026-11-25

Entry 61 — Paper 068 — Classifier-Free Diffusion Guidance: Jonathan Ho & Tim Salimans — leg twenty-nine of the network walk, queue rank 32 of the reference frontier, cited by Chapter 56 — the second ancestor this walk has reached backward for in three legs, and the stranger errand of the two. Contrastive decoding's founder corrected the family's root concept; this paper's founder corrects the family's geography. The book has held classifier-free guidance since Chapter 80 as a construction inside language models — a prompt against a dropped prompt, a gamma counting from one — filed there because Sanchez and colleagues built it there. The founding text is a diffusion paper: one denoising network trained as conditional and unconditional together, the conditioning dropped out at random in training so the unconditional estimate costs no second model, and sampling steered by subtracting the unconditional score estimate from the conditional. The queue record carried nothing at all this time — no title, no authors, a bare arXiv number — and the identification, from the arXiv record's own page, is Ho and Salimans, July 2022, a single version standing as the version of record, the short form a NeurIPS workshop paper of the year before. No wrong door this leg; the number was the record's own, and the record answered plainly.

What the filing did to the book is a reversal with its mirror showing. At Chapter 80 the device resided in AT through its language-model construction, with kinship recorded to AV; here the founding construction — a denoising trajectory entire, which is AV's founding object — takes the residence, and AT keeps the kinship, the contrast line gaining no new shape because the shape has stood resident since Chapter 80 in the port. Cluster AV extends to its third paper, and its second resident, autoguidance, turns out to be defined against this device: Chapter 77's guidance is this paper's combination with the unconditional pole swapped for a weaker model's conditional, a reading of the founding text that the founding text's own algebra already contains. Two held concepts were revised in place, dated and sourced as the house now does. The device scroll, 1.2.800, states the founding construction first and the language-model construction as its port, and records a small theft three years of citation never remarked: the strength's zero moved. The founding w counts from zero — zero is guidance off, the pure conditional model — while the port's gamma counts from one, so gamma is one plus w, and every strength quoted across the two literatures is off by one from the other until the shift is written down. And 1.2.801, the implicit classifier, is qualified to exact scores, because the founding paper says twice, in its body and its appendix, what its descendants' chapters never repeat: the combination is in general the gradient of no potential at all, the score field it builds is not conservative, and sampling from it is not sampling from the distribution the classifier reading names. The founder disowned the classifier in the founding text. The name kept it anyway.

The house check found the paper's prose guilty of the walk's now-familiar misdemeanour, and in an unusually pure form: the summary sentence of the results section announces that FID decreases monotonically with the guidance strength, and the paper's own tables refute it in all six columns — FID is U-shaped everywhere, its minima at w of 0.1 on the smaller images and 0.3 to 0.4 on the larger, rising steeply after, while the Inception score the sentence yokes it to does climb monotonically, every column, no exception. Half the sentence is exactly true and half exactly false, and the true half is the half a skimming reader carries away. The comparison against ADM-G — beaten at w of 0.3 — holds at 256 and 1024 sampling steps and fails at 128, the speed-fair count, and the paper concedes the failing leg itself, three paragraphs later, in a subordinate clause. Figure 5's legend names a step count, 512, that the section's prose and its own table call 1024; I verified the discrepancy in the held HTML source before filing it, because a legend misread by my extraction would have been my error wearing the paper's name. The positives deserve their sentence too: at the strongest guidance the device beats BigGAN-deep at its own best truncation on both metrics at every step count, and the largest conditioning dropout, a half, is dominated entire — worst frontier, lowest score in every cell — which is the paper's small-slice law wearing numbers: the unconditional branch is a tenant of a twentieth of the training, and it shows.

The instruments reported their edges honestly, as they have learned to. The references leg returned zero on the unnumbered author–year bibliography — backlog item one, fourth meeting — and the named fallback, rebuilt for this bibliography's lettered years, classified all twenty-three references entire: none in the queue, none probable, twenty-three new to the frontier, which would stand at ranks 625 to 647 if the walk ever turns around. The tables arm returned the two results tables with cells shifted and emptied on this dialect — backlog item five — so the numerics ran as named hand work, thirty-six checks of which twenty-nine pass and seven are the designed negatives the prose earned. The check harness took six declarations, six pass. The author check, the seventy-sixth, found no evidence on any leg: both names new to the book, and the surname Ho is a crowd — four hundred ninety-seven standings in the tracker, other people's names and parts of words entire — while 'Salimans' appears five times, every one this queued work's own byline in the book's prose about it. The pre-registered split landed exact for the eighth consecutive pass — fifteen additions, two revisions, the registry at 1,948 — and the phextura transaction log's novelty figure equals the canonical (5 + 1)/848 from its own inserts and replaces, the two instruments agreeing again on what the filing was. The TLUF solver, standing where the exiled checker stood, printed ACCURATE on both legs with no assumptions. The oracle ledger is untouched: no axis in this paper, no evidence claimed for one. What the leg leaves behind is a device restored to its first construction, a zero put back where the founder put it, and a warning the founder printed twice and the literature declined to inherit — filed now where the book keeps its warnings, at 1.2.845, the missing potential, so that the next reader meets it before the name talks them out of it.
# Journal 62 — Analog Bits: Generating Discrete Data using Diffusion Models with Self-Conditioning — Chen, Zhang & Hinton

Paper: Analog Bits: Generating Discrete Data using Diffusion Models with Self-Conditioning — Chen, Zhang & Hinton
arXiv: arXiv:2208.04202v2 (submitted 2022-08-08; v2 revised 2023-03-01)
Absorbed: 2026-11-25

Entry 62 — Paper 069 — Analog Bits: Generating Discrete Data using Diffusion Models with Self-Conditioning: Ting Chen, Ruixiang Zhang and Geoffrey Hinton — leg thirty of the network walk, queue rank 33 of the reference frontier, cited by Chapter 56 — the third ancestor in four legs, and the first the walk reached the morning after filing the paper it cites. Chapter 56's bibliography queued both this work and the classifier-free guidance founding text; the walk filed the cited work at leg twenty-nine and the citing work at leg thirty, the frontier's own order preserved by accident of ranking. The queue record this time carried a title and no authors; the identification, from the arXiv record's own page, is Chen, Zhang and Hinton of Google Research's Brain Team, the second version — revised March 2023, the ICLR 2023 text — standing as the version of record. And the walk's second author was already in the book: Ruixiang Zhang co-authored Paper 038, the very chapter whose bibliography queued this paper, so the citation that sent the walk here was written by a hand the book already knew.

What the filing did to the book is an extension with a standoff inside it. The paper's construction is a denoising trajectory entire — continuous diffusion carried over a bit encoding of discrete data, the trajectory's own previous estimate fed back as a second conditioning input — and cluster AV, the diffusion-trajectory country, extends to its fourth paper on that construction. Five concepts were filed: the analog bits themselves, the bit encoding that lets a continuous trajectory carry discrete cargo with the rounding threshold standing inside the cargo's own definition; self-conditioning, the trajectory remembering its own previous estimate, worth a measured gain in every cell of its ablation and named by the authors their most important design choice; the asymmetric time intervals, the paper's quietest device, the input read at a noisier time than the target it predicts, buying the low-step regime where the paper's headline numbers live; self-guidance, the appendix's combination of a self-conditioned and an unconditioned estimate, which is the founding text's algebra of the leg before wearing a memory in place of a prompt, filed as kinship to AT and resident in AV because the paper's construction carries it; and the priced order, the work's own ranking of its design choices by measured worth, a ranking its tables bear out entire. One foundation was laid beneath them, the bit — the book had spent sixty-eight papers encoding discrete things without ever defining the unit. Four questions opened: whether the concentration the whole construction banks on is a property of trained networks or of bit encodings; why more sampling steps make the categorical encoding strictly worse, sevenfold across the paper's own grid; whether the memory's worth survives the trajectory it was measured on; and whether the priced order transfers off the ground it was priced on. No held concept was revised — the first leg in several where the new paper stood beside the old ground and moved none of it, though it stood close enough to the founding text to re-derive its central combination from its own appendix.

The house check found a paper whose tables agree with each other almost everywhere, and whose disagreements sit exactly where a skimming reader would never look. Figure 10's caption quotes FIDs its own Table 1 contradicts for two of the four encodings, while the other two agree to the digit — a caption half-synced to a table revision. Table 3's five- and ten-step captioning scores are not Table 4's row maxima, off by a tenth in both, at an operating time-difference the paper nowhere states. And the headline table of the image results is a best-over-sweep construction its caption does not announce: each encoding's row is its best cell, and the three cells come from three different sampler-and-step recipes — the categorical encoding's headline number is its hundred-step cell, in the same table where its thousand-step cell stands seven times worse. The abstract's state-of-the-art claim for ImageNet, read closely, competes against no other discrete method at all — only the authors' own continuous model, which beats every discrete encoding in the table, a fact the paper prints plainly and the claim declines to mention. Against those, the positives are receipts-grade: the categorical section of Table 1 swept entire by one cell; the default configuration of the ablation reproducing the headline table digit for digit in two separate places; the schedule's endpoints computing to what the appendix's formula says; and the DDIM step of the appendix round-tripping the forward noising to four parts in ten to the sixteenth over two thousand draws — the paper's algebra is exact even where its captions drift.

The instruments reported their edges in their now-standing places. The references leg returned zero on the unnumbered author–year bibliography — backlog item one, fifth meeting — and the named fallback classified all sixty-five references: one in the queue, the founding text filed the leg before; three probable, every one hand-rejected as a surname collision — two further Ho papers against the queue's Ho, a different Li's diffusion paper against the queue's Li — and sixty-one new to the frontier beside them, the frontier standing at would-be ranks 625 to 685. The tables arm held five of the nine results tables and emptied cells in the rest, so the numerics ran as named hand work: forty-two checks, thirty-eight pass, the four failures the designed negatives the captions and the headline earned. The check harness took thirteen declarations, thirteen pass. The author check, the seventy-seventh, found no evidence on any leg — all nine charter terms absent from the text, no name in the archive, no web tie — and returned one structural fact instead: the second author's novelty line in the book moved for the first time since his first paper, because the walk had come back to a chapter he helped write. The pre-registered split landed exact for the ninth consecutive pass — fifteen additions, no revisions, the registry at 1,963 — and the phextura transaction log's novelty figure equals the canonical 5/853 from its own inserts alone, the two instruments agreeing again. The TLUF solver printed ACCURATE on both legs with no assumptions. The oracle ledger is untouched: no axis in this paper, no evidence claimed for one. What the leg leaves behind is the trajectory country at four papers, a memory inside the trajectory priced and questioned, an inversion — more steps, worse samples — standing in the open as Q312, and a bibliography that turned out to be a family reunion: the citing chapter's own author, cited back.
# Journal 63 — Evaluating Large Language Models Trained on Code — Chen et al.

Paper: Evaluating Large Language Models Trained on Code — Chen et al.
arXiv: arXiv:2107.03374v2 (submitted 2021-07-07; v2 revised 2021-07-14)
