Entry 63 — Paper 070 — Evaluating Large Language Models Trained on Code: Mark Chen, Jerry Tworek, Heewoo Jun, Qiming Yuan, Henrique Ponde de Oliveira Pinto, Jared Kaplan, Harri Edwards, Yuri Burda, Nicholas Joseph, Greg Brockman, Alex Ray, Raul Puri, Gretchen Krueger, Michael Petrov, Heidy Khlaaf, Girish Sastry, Pamela Mishkin, Brooke Chan, Scott Gray, Nick Ryder, Mikhail Pavlov, Alethea Power, Lukasz Kaiser, Mohammad Bavarian, Clemens Winter, Philippe Tillet, Felipe Petroski Such, Dave Cummings, Matthias Plappert, Fotios Chantzis, Elizabeth Barnes, Ariel Herbert-Voss, William Hebgen Guss, Alex Nichol, Alex Paino, Nikolas Tezak, Jie Tang, Igor Babuschkin, Suchir Balaji, Shantanu Jain, William Saunders, Christopher Hesse, Andrew N. Carr, Jan Leike, Josh Achiam, Vedant Misra, Evan Morikawa, Alec Radford, Matthew Knight, Miles Brundage, Mira Murati, Katie Mayer, Peter Welinder, Bob McGrew, Dario Amodei, Sam McCandlish, Ilya Sutskever and Wojciech Zaremba — leg thirty-one of the network walk, queue rank 34 of the reference frontier, cited by Chapter 56. The queue record carried neither title nor byline this time — an identifier and a citing chapter, nothing more — and the identification stands from the arXiv record itself: the Codex paper, fifty-eight authors of OpenAI, the second version of July 2021 standing as the version of record. It is the largest byline the book has taken in, and every one of the fifty-eight is new to it.

What the filing did to the book is to complete the examination country's founding, backwards, as the walk keeps doing. Chapter 83 filed the grader with no table of its own; Chapter 84 filed this table's descendant, audited to eighty times its depth; this chapter files the table itself — 164 programming problems written by hand because the training corpus already holds the wild's problem sets, authorship itself spent as the anti-contamination defense. Cluster AY extends to its sixth paper on the country's own definition, and the infrastructure founding was weighed under Chapter 84's restated condition and declined a third time: the work has a table, and its sandbox is the table's room, not an interface offered to others. Seven concepts were filed: the executed verdict, correctness by running the candidate against unit tests, displacing the match verdicts the book filed at its start; pass@k, the any-of-k measure with its unbiased estimator, the units every later resident of the country reports in; the hand-written examination itself; the sandbox, the verdict's execution room, built to survive the judged; the oracle-free choice, the thirty-three points between the best deployable pick and the pick the tests would make; the chain decay, capability divided by two to three for every clause chained onto a specification; and the withheld capability, misalignment given its first operational definition in the book — capable of the thing and doing otherwise, the gap measured in an appendix and growing with scale. No foundation was laid and no held concept revised: the audit of Chapter 84 had read this table's descendant faithfully enough that the ancestor, arriving five chapters later, moves nothing. Four questions opened: whether any signal at the moment of choice can close the oracle gap; whether the chain tax is the model class's or the synthetic blocks' independence; whether the withheld-capability gap is the data's price or the objective's shape; and whether an executed verdict can be manufactured at the founding's honesty, or is always either small and hand-made or large and inherited. Cluster J was weighed a seventeenth time and not joined — and this weighing came nearest since the crossing in a new place: the work's self-filter really does spend a verdict, the model's own samples judged by the tests and the survivors made the next model's curriculum. But the spending lands one stage up and one run later, at the data's gate; inside any judged computation no verdict is consulted, and around the computation is not inside it. The boundary holds at the locus, and the weighing testifies on Q288 as narrowed.

