What the filing did to the book is to give cluster AR its ninth paper, and with it the filtration theory the cluster's eight earlier papers are built on: the Bruhat filtration entered the tracker as Paper 036's machinery — a smooth filtration here, a transversal refinement there, a distribution-valued sibling in a third place — and this filing holds the construction whole, at the source all three name. Eleven concepts were filed: the relative Schwartz space and tempered distributions, the smooth sections flat on a closed complement and their strong dual, with Borel's theorem as the point case where flatness at one point exhausts the formal power series; tempered distributions supported on a submanifold, with the transversal degree, the filtration by normal order, exhaustive, a filtered module over the differential operators, the hyperplane model case a sum of layers; the stratification filtration and its graded object, Theorem 3.1's exact computation and Theorem 3.4's orbit form, the graded module the sum of the strata's distribution duals; the Bruhat filtration of the smooth principal series, Theorem 4.1 — the ledger's thousandth concept, the founding form of the filtration three filed chapters descend from; the graded pieces over a Bruhat cell, the tensor-product form of Lemmas 4.2 to 4.4, each cell's contribution finitely layered over its own function ring; the twisted regular representation and its homology, Theorem 5.6's vanishing engine — finite, bounded by the dimension, and zero unless the character is central-trivial with vanishing real part, proved by the Fourier transform in the abelian case and downward induction through the centre; the dual vanishing and the one-dimensional Whittaker homology, Theorem 5.12 with Proposition 5.13 and Corollary 5.14 — on the open cell exactly one functional, the Jacquet integral; Whittaker vectors for smooth principal series, Theorem 6.1's count — zero off the purely imaginary characters, the fibre's dimension on them — wi